  "worked_solution": "First, use the identity $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) & =(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )(1+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }) \\\\  & =(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta +1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we expand the parentheses in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )(1+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
